==============================================================================
PART 3 — crossed product +q shift; a as input not output
==============================================================================

[i] +q (observer energy) shift:
    modular operator Delta^{it} = exp(i t (H_mod + q)); KMS period beta = 2pi/kappa.
    beta is the GENERATOR's flow period, set by kappa=H, INDEPENDENT of the additive q.
    => the type II_1 dressing keeps the KMS/modular temperature at T_GH=H/2pi (boost time).
    (q makes the trace FINITE -> type II_1, and shifts entropy by <q>, but not the temp.)

[ii] a is INPUT (which worldline), not OUTPUT (the algebra fixes beta=2pi/H, generator=boost):
     every a>0 is some boost orbit's redshift; all carry the SAME modular data.
     => the algebra cannot 'predict' a particular a (hence cannot predict a0).

[iii] a0 number = cH_Lambda/Z. Algebra gives the a~H CROSSOVER (scale H = INPUT) and
      reproduces S=A/4G (max-entropy=GH) but does NOT derive a0's coefficient Z.
      Closing that needs the UNPROVEN state-level dictionary phi (agentUU). => NOT derivational.

[crossover numerics] T_DL(a)/T_GH at a=0,H,5.789H,33.5^.5 H:
     a/H=  0.0000:  T_DL/T_GH = sqrt(1+(a/H)^2) = 1.000000
     a/H=  1.0000:  T_DL/T_GH = sqrt(1+(a/H)^2) = 1.414214
     a/H=  5.7888:  T_DL/T_GH = sqrt(1+(a/H)^2) = 5.874549
     a/H=  5.7879:  T_DL/T_GH = sqrt(1+(a/H)^2) = 5.873662

[CONCLUSION PART 3]
 The crossed-product +q dressing PRESERVES the modular/KMS temperature at the boost value
 (beta=2pi/H); Tolman re-clocking on a boost orbit of acceleration a gives EXACTLY T_DL(a).
 a is an INPUT (choice of worldline), the crossover scale is H (INPUT). The algebra
 REPRODUCES the semiclassical DL temperature and S=A/4G but DERIVES neither a0's scale
 nor its coefficient Z. STRUCTURAL bridge confirmed; derivational claim REFUTED.
